<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH CONSTRUCTION GROWTH SEEN ABATING IN 1998.</title>
<headline>DUTCH CONSTRUCTION GROWTH SEEN ABATING IN 1998.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volume growth of the Dutch construction sector is expected to slow to one percent from more than two in 1997 despite favourable general economic trends, the Economic Institute for the Building sector (EIB) said on Friday.</p>
<p>A survey by the institute showed volumes in the markets for large buildings and infrastructural projects are expected to expand by one to four percent in 1998.</p>
<p>But the housing construction sector is seen shrinking by three percent next year, after a 3.5 percent rise in 1997, as fewer building permits have been awarded, the EIB said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
